Never download executable code at runtime (Chromium 156, Linux desktop)

Chromium downloads and loads several pieces of executable code at runtime
through the component updater (update.googleapis.com) or from other
Google-hosted locations. This patch removes every such path that is active
in a non-Google-branded Linux build, while leaving data-only components
(lists, configs, ML weights) and user-initiated extension installs alone:

  * Widevine CDM          - libwidevinecdm.so  (component "WidevineCdm")
                            A CDM installed on the system is still found via
                            the bundled dir (bundle_widevine_cdm=true) or the
                            hint file $USERDATA/WidevineCdm/latest-component-
                            updated-widevine-cdm ({"Path": "<dir>"}).
  * SODA                  - libsoda.so + language packs (Live Caption,
                            on-device Web Speech, Dictation). Reported as
                            unsupported, so the UI does not offer it.
  * Screen AI             - libchromescreenai.so (PDF OCR, main-content
                            extraction for Reading Mode).
  * TranslateKit          - libtranslatekit.so (Translator / LanguageDetector
                            web APIs). --translate-kit-binary-path still works.
  * WASM TTS engine       - bindings_main.wasm + JS in a component extension
                            (natural voices for Reading Mode / Read Aloud).
  * Dictation Connector   - JS component extension (feature off by default).
  * Indigo                - content_script.js injected into pages (off by
                            default).
  * AIM Eligibility       - component-updated replacement of the bundled
                            omnibox "AI Mode" eligibility component extension.
                            The bundled copy keeps being used, the AI Mode
                            button is not affected.
  * DevTools remote front-end - devtools://devtools/remote/... fetched from
                            chrome-devtools-frontend.appspot.com and run in the
                            privileged devtools:// origin (used when inspecting
                            remote targets with a different version).

The gates are placed in the Register*() functions of the individual
installers (not in registration.cc) so that the on-demand registration paths
(SODA installer, Screen AI downloader, TranslateKit installer_impl, Reading
Mode) are covered as well and the patch does not conflict with other patches
that edit registration.cc. All edited code is compiled identically in the
default GN configuration and with enable_screen_ai_service=false /
build_with_tflite_lib=false / build_with_internal_optimization_guide=false
(files that are not built in a configuration are simply not compiled).
Function bodies are replaced rather than preceded by an early return because
Chromium builds with -Wunreachable-code-aggressive.

